WEBVTT

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.760
Getting myself psyched for the day is an important part of my routine.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.960
That you, Mom? I'll be down for breakfast in a bit.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.960
Huh? What're you blabbering about?

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.100
I'm coming in, Takayama.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.220
D-Derailment!

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.720
Wow. Do you even need to train?

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.390
Dummy!

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:48.850
In battle, a few millimeters' difference can mean the difference between victory and defeat!

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:53.230
So you train for victory, Sakurai?

00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:00.490
Damn, you just wallow in your pacifist stupor, don't you?

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:04.910
Looks like I've gotta staple your balls back on for you!

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.800
Too slow!

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.880
Hold on a second!

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.590
Mercy is wasted on the evil!

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.600
What "evil" are you talking about?

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:29.770
You looked up my skirt for a second just now.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.060
Sexual harassment is big-time evil, buster!

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:55.330
So Takayama joined you for training this morning?

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.170
It's a requirement for those in the Public Security Force.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:03.840
Oh, this?

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.140
Cute, isn't it?

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:10.140
Hitomi and I were in town and found this great shop.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.390
Wanna come with us sometime?

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:13.900
Not that.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.770
I just don't get it.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:20.230
Why do I have to partner with that pacifist buffoon just to get permission for arms training?

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:22.700
Peace is a lovely thing!

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.950
When the power of love overcomes the love of power, no?

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:36.130
Where'd you get that, Takayama?

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:36.830
Huh?

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.420
Oh, uh, it's no big deal.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.340
But it is.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:52.430
There.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.730
I'll make us some tea.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.020
Th-Thanks.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:03.400
E-Eyes to yourself!

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.360
Sasshou? She the one we helped?

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.910
Our school's having a trip tomorrow to welcome the new students,

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.290
so we were discussing it.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.250
Hey, Takayama.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.290
Wh-What?

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:19.250
I guess I should thank you for training with me this morning.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.340
It helped me let off some steam.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:25.720
The JNR Ashio Line?

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:33.140
It's the line that runs from Kiryu, Gunma to that famous mining town, Ashio in Tochigi.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.850
But why are you taking the Ashio Line?

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:39.360
Well, as a treat for future JNR employees,

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:45.490
they're giving us a special ride from Mato to Ashio-Honzan,

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:50.490
a route exclusive to freight trains!

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.490
And on a KiHa 52!

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:02.210
It's truly the symbol of JNR during its years in the economic boom!

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:06.470
Its twin engines are unstoppable,
cutting across all mountains and valleys!

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.930
Everyone, can I have your attention?

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:16.390
That criminal who set up a bomb in
Tokyo Station apparently had an accomplice.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.360
Just leave it to me!

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.690
I swear, I'll bring this crook to justice!

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:29.070
I think Hitomi's team can handle the investigation herself.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.700
Of course.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.120
We'll operate as normal.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.500
But be on your guard.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.540
I guess we should split into pairs and patrol, then.

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:44.210
Sakurai's not here yet, so I'll wait for her.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:47.050
Koumi and Iwaizumi, you go on ahead.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:49.220
What's keeping Aoi?

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.470
She's talking with Ms. Iida.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:53.100
Something's up, don't you think?

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.100
She's been on edge all morning.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.730
Well, we're off, Deputy!

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:05.570
Yeah, Takayama, you're the deputy leader.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:08.820
You have to pay attention to everyone.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.660
Y-Yeah.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:13.030
Sorry I took so long.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:15.580
No kidding.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:20.710
Wait, was Ms. Iida chewing you out about this morning?

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:22.250
No.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.800
Seriously, though, the women in the PSF can take men on in a fight.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.510
I was so ready to blast a name for myself!

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.640
Damn it!

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:40.600
I-I'm terribly sorry, sir!

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.730
You aren't hurt, are you?

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.190
I'm so, so sorry!

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.440
You too, Sakurai!

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:49.280
Takayama.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.490
Follow him.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:52.530
H-Hey!

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:59.700
What are you up to now?

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:01.660
That's the bomber's accomplice.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.290
The bomber?

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:05.500
The guy in the photo this morning.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:06.340
What?

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:07.670
You're kidding!

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.380
I'm sure of it.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:10.840
That was the guy in the photo.

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:14.090
He must have been watching the office.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:15.050
Hey!

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.440
Takayama?

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:25.690
The train is leaving.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:27.610
Please step back.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.320
The train is leaving.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:36.320
Thank you for using the Takasaki Line.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:40.370
This is the local train bound for Takasaki Station.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:44.500
We will be stopping at all stations.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.800
This is bad. We should head back.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.760
As long as we capture the criminal, everything'll be A-OK!

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.720
No, it won't be!

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:02.310
Anyway, we at least should contact Ms. Iida.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:04.140
Whatever.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:07.810
I'll chase him, even if I have to do it myself.

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:14.400
What?

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.740
Yeah, I took them off.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.320
I got a run in them during training this morning.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:21.490
Sorry.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:22.950
It's from Sasshou.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.000
Just confirming what time we meet up tomorrow.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.080
For that freight line thingy?

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.670
Not the "freight line," the Ashio Line.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:32.380
Tomayto, tomahto.

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:37.510
Just don't infect me with your clumsiness.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:51.980
I'm sorry for just leaving like that.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:53.480
Tell me where you are now.

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:54.780
Right.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.030
We're on the Ryomo Line headed for Maebashi.

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:01.450
Sakurai's certain this is the guy from the photo.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:03.540
What do you think, Takayama?

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.790
I'd like to trust Sakurai's judgment.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.710
Oh?

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:09.750
Well, then.

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:12.420
You have permission to continue tailing him.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:15.840
However, you must leave his arrest to Hitomi and her men.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.340
I'll send them your way.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:24.470
He'll see you!

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:27.100
So? What'd Ms. Iida say?

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:28.940
We have permission to tail him.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:32.440
Now we just have to time our arrest right.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.940
That's not our job.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.940
We have to wait for backup.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:37.950
What?!

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:42.660
We can do this ourselves!

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.990
Sakurai, whatвЂ”

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.540
Are you sure about this, Ms. Iida?

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:53.000
Of all people, you gave Sakurai a gun.

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:59.970
She insisted that it was too dangerous to go unarmed with the bomber's accomplice on the loose.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:05.510
And I was sure you'd make the right decision.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:06.430
Huh?

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:10.810
I knew you wouldn't be able to leave Sakurai alone today.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:13.190
So she's in your hands, Deputy.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.700
When's this backup supposed to get here, Takayama?

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.030
Sakurai.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:23.820
Wh-What?

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.200
I trust you.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.040
Not that I can do much else, though.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:47.140
The cars are slowly emptying.

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:50.140
We might not be able to tail him much longer.

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:54.100
Oh, KiHa 40...

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:56.900
I wish I could enjoy riding you more.

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:12.000
There's even a line that goes all the way out in the mountains, huh?

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.210
Yeah.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:15.460
The rails connect us all.

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:18.210
They'll take you wherever you want in Japan.

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:35.400
You okay?

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:37.980
Yeah!

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:41.030
Don't mind me!

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:45.410
Look out!

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.250
Get back here!

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.560
Nice, Takayama!

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:15.390
Stop!

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:23.780
Hold it!

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:25.490
Don't shoot, Sakurai!

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:30.830
I don't need this to take him down!

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.880
Hey, Sakurai!

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:47.010
Ms. Iida? It's Takayama.

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:50.260
I'm sorry. We were spotted,
and now the criminal's on the run.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:13:59.650
No service, huh?

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:03.530
Did she really chase him all the way into the mountains?

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.950
Is he holed up in there?

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.820
Man, I really hate the dark.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.950
Takayama's my unlucky charm, I swear.

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:17.580
Why didn't you chase after me?

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:19.210
Dummy.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.510
An underground railway?

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:35.520
The rails connect us all, huh?

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:40.230
If I stay here, will Takayama find me?

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.020
Not that I need him to come.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:46.030
I can just walk back.

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.450
Sakurai!

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.670
Takayama?

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.010
If someone enters that shaft,

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:12.720
it sets off an alarm in the closest station, Kobe.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:17.020
A cargo train just happened to pass by when I hatched my hunch.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.230
Took you long enough.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:20.730
It's all good.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.520
As long as you're safe, Sakurai.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:30.240
The appropriate PSF division is taking over the search.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:32.280
We'll head back to Tokyo tomorrow morning.

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:33.450
No.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:36.790
I'm catching this criminal!

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:38.080
You don't have to worry.

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:42.120
The local PSF will find him.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:44.630
And you're okay with that, Takayama?

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:48.460
It's not our job to chase criminals, is it?

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:54.300
What?

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:56.970
At least wear this.

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:59.100
Why would I wear <i>your</i> вЂ”

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:09.990
You're bigger than me, huh, Takayama?

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.240
You're just slender, Sakurai.

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:15.240
And just as wild, I suppose.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.950
I'm not wild.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:19.160
I take all my training seriously.

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:21.120
And my dad's a police officer.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:26.460
So that's how you can hold one of these like it's nothing, huh?

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.210
You shaking?

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:29.920
Pathetic.

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:32.470
My dad's just an office worker.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:37.550
It was my dad's dream for me to join the police.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:41.480
So he trained me in self-defense, marksmanship, and other stuff.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.560
Takayama?

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:50.400
I'm sorry I caused you trouble.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.320
You missed your trip because of me, too.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.320
Huh?

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:54.660
Wh-What?

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:57.870
I, uh, wasn't expecting you to say that.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:58.870
What?

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:01.950
I can admit when things are my fault, you know!

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:04.460
Sakurai, look down! Down!

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:09.090
Quit staring!

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:45.500
You're sure it was him, Sakurai?

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:46.580
Oh yeah!

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:50.170
There he is!

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:54.590
We're from the Tokyo Central PSF Office, Fourth Peacekeepers Squad!

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.170
Give it up!

00:17:58.720 --> 00:17:59.970
Stop right there!

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:05.520
What's wrong?

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:06.810
It's a bomb!

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.540
The track!

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:27.330
Are you okay, Sakurai?

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:29.670
Doesn't even hurt.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:31.790
We've gotta go after him!

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:38.630
The safety of the rails matters more than some criminal.

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:41.390
We're the JNR Public Security Force.

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:50.060
If only we could cut that wire.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.270
What're you talking about?

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:55.400
It's used to detect rockfalls.

00:18:55.400 --> 00:19:00.410
Cutting it would activate the alarm and alert the conductor to danger ahead.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.740
We might be able to stop the train.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:05.240
Crap!

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:06.830
We have to do something fast!

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:10.210
I'll shoot it.

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.210
I just have to cut the wire, right?

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:14.750
But...

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:17.460
You trust me, right?

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:19.590
Sakurai.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:23.100
It's in your hands.

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:30.850
Takayama.

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.400
Let's get off the tracks! It's too dangerous!

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:38.280
Takayama, crouch in front of me!

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:41.360
My right arm's shaking too much to get a good shot!

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:42.360
Hurry!

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:42.910
Huh?

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.330
L-Like this?

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:56.550
You move even an inch and I'll put one between your eyes.

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:28.790
It stopped.

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:35.750
Sakurai?

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:38.250
Just stay still.

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:41.380
You move and you're dead.

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:54.900
I'm very sorry for all the trouble caused!

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.860
I'm very sorry.

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:05.910
The local PSF caught the man, so there's no need to worry.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:14.250
I can't commend everything you did,
but thanks to you two we avoided a great accident.

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:15.830
Good work.

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:18.040
Thank you!

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:20.800
And despite her sour face,
Sakurai is indeed very sorryвЂ”

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:21.760
Hands off!

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:24.760
Such a tiny piece of cloth.

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:28.260
Yet there's a world of difference
between wearing and not wearing it.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:32.850
We're not the police, you know?

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:36.140
We of the PSF are JNR employees.

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:40.020
Our customers' safety should always come first.

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:43.490
Are you starting to get it now?

00:21:43.490 --> 00:21:45.780
Why I chose Takayama?

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.410
I formally request permission for training.

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:52.830
I'm going to train this spineless coward from the ground up so he's fit for duty.

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:58.580
Takayama's kind-hearted, not spineless.

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:02.920
It's that bit of him that invites women to dote on him that makes him spineless!

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:05.550
You're too nice, Haruka!

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:07.970
Aren't you just too tough, Aoi?

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:09.510
Of course not!

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:43.900
It's the museum with a collection spanning all Japanese transportation methods,

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:48.030
opened to commemorate the 50th
anniversary of Japan's railway system,

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:52.240
which later transfered locations to the old Manseibashi Station building!

00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:53.820
Yes, the Transportation Museum!

00:23:54.320 --> 00:23:55.450
Wait, why am I saying this?

00:23:55.780 --> 00:23:57.620
Where'd that idiot Takayama go?

00:23:57.620 --> 00:24:02.120
I'm sorry, Aoi. Takayama's running for his life.

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:06.090
Rail Wars, Episode Six: I'll Protect You.

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:07.840
I'm so embarrassed!

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:09.300
But I'll do my best!
